  CUP's actual peer review process:
  — Supplementary materials are uploaded through the
     SAME submission system used for the original
     manuscript (Cambridge Core, ScholarOne, or
     Editorial Manager)
  — Reviewers may REQUEST additional detail, but
     never the complete training corpus
  — Source code sharing is done through GitHub or
     institutional repositories, NOT through email
     portals
  — The review timeline is 30-60 days for response,
     not 16 days
  — Failure to provide supplementary detail results in
     a REQUEST for revision, not automatic rejection

  If you receive an email requesting complete training
  data samples or model weights through a portal,
  it is a phishing attempt targeting academic authors.

